From: RTSP-on-GE development <development@localhost>
Subject: [PROPOSED] mf: retain late sink demand until stopped sources restart

After natural EOS, SAR can queue a request after the Session's final flush.
Pulling a stopped source returns MF_E_MEDIA_SOURCE_WRONGSTATE while the
intervening transforms retain their output requests. Later preroll adds
demand but sees an already outstanding transform pull, so audio never restarts.

Keep the sink demand during stop/stopped-start gaps using the existing
RESTARTING flag. Re-prime at the all-sources-started barrier before either
preroll or ordinary clock start. Do not reset EOS generations again, change
timeouts, or retry failed reads/seeks. This is a proposal, not an active pin.

--- a/dlls/mf/session.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/session.c
@@ -3374,6 +3374,12 @@
             }
             session_set_presentation_clock(session);
 
+            if (session->presentation.flags & SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING)
+            {
+                session->presentation.flags &= ~SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING;
+                session_flush_sinks(session);
+            }
+
             if (session->presentation.rate != 0.0f && (session->presentation.flags & SESSION_FLAG_NEEDS_PREROLL)
                     && session_is_output_nodes_state(session, OBJ_STATE_STOPPED))
             {
@@ -3411,12 +3417,6 @@
             }
             else
             {
-                if (session->presentation.flags & SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING)
-                {
-                    session->presentation.flags &= ~SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING;
-                    session_flush_sinks(session);
-                }
-
                 if (SUCCEEDED(hr = session_start_clock(session)))
                 {
                     /* If sinks are already started, start session immediately. This can happen when doing a
@@ -4372,6 +4372,17 @@
     }
 
     sink_node->u.sink.requests++;
+    /* Late sink demand can outlive EOS/Stop. Do not strand transform requests
+     * on a stopped source. Retain the demand for the all-sources-started
+     * barrier, including restarts which need to preroll the sinks again. */
+    if (session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_STOPPING_SINKS
+            || session->command_state == COMMAND_STATE_STOPPING_SOURCES
+            || (session->state == SESSION_STATE_STOPPED
+                && !session_is_source_nodes_state(session, OBJ_STATE_STARTED)))
+    {
+        session->presentation.flags |= SESSION_FLAG_RESTARTING;
+        return;
+    }
     /* Keep sink demand while stopped seek sources restart. Pulling now can
      * leave a transform request stranded after MF_E_MEDIA_SOURCE_WRONGSTATE.
      * The all-sources-started barrier clears RESTARTING before re-priming. */
